      "why": "iterative is the lowest-area family (single shared datapath, no pipeline registers). It is the only family that can plausibly meet the >=1 MSPS throughput constraint at minimal area, since its throughput = Fmax (1 result/cycle at the micro-rotation level is not applicable; it produces 1 result every N+3 cycles, so throughput = Fmax/(N+3)). For small N (4-8) and modest data_width, Fmax can be high enough that Fmax/(N+3) >= 1 MSPS. The error constraint (<= 2^-10) is met by n_iter >= ~10-12 with data_width >= 12. I narrow data_width to 10-16 and n_iter to 4-16 to focus on the feasible region where both constraints can be satisfied with minimal area."
    }
